{
  "_about": "The ONE source of the 'what we can produce' page (plan 43.4, Trust lane item 2, contract rules 7 and 8). Every row is a code fact under test (internal/api/produce_test.go): account rows ARE the GDPR export's sections and their fields (account_export_sections.go), retention rows ARE the retention job's policies (retention.go), backup periods are deploy/scripts/pg-backup.sh's, every table and column named exists in the migrated schema, the SSE-C row's columns are what a Private bucket's object row holds (proved by a write). Mode names and sentences are never here: the page renders modes.json through internal/modes. A row with requires_flag is rendered only while that flag is ON globally. Change the code and this file together.",
